Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
11.5 [BSc] How do I verify no-signalling through the invariance of reduced \
states?\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9947777788245735`*^9},ExpressionUUID->"dc2e9602-893c-e747-9df3-\
64c5ae2c6f94"],

Cell["\<\
Whatever Bob does to his qubit alone, Alice\[CloseCurlyQuote]s reduced state \
is unchanged: for a unitary because the unitary and its adjoint meet under \
the trace over Bob\[CloseCurlyQuote]s factor, and for a measurement Bob does \
not report because the non-selective L\[UDoubleDot]ders sum contracts to the \
same thing. Since Alice\[CloseCurlyQuote]s statistics are fixed by her \
reduced state, no choice Bob makes can carry information to her. The claim is \
linear in the joint state, so a generic  4\[Times]4 array with nothing \
assumed about it already settles it for every state.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9947778112054615`*^9, 3.994777822605753*^9}, 
   3.994777855194214*^9},ExpressionUUID->"86b6dd85-01ae-fc4f-9336-\
e8d002e82c05"],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["WL:",
 FontWeight->"Bold"]], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.99477790257592*^9, 
  3.9947779060826073`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5a26c3e1-f961-3340-95f8-\
9a8ffe15b3ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Take a generic two-qubit operator and its reduction over ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["B", TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "ed387d51-3368-bd4b-803c-8e377d2b45e0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.994777915526903*^9, 
  3.994777925148945*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"b79def93-f7d1-a642-92f9-\
98ee6636518d"],

